      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُفَافٌ</span></b>  <i>What is dry</i> of a thing that one has
dried. (K.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِعْزِلْ جُفَافَهُ مِنْ رَطْبِهِ</span> [<i>Put
thou apart what is dry thereof from what is fresh
and moist thereof</i>]. (TA.)

